* ki	KI	tense default
* tei	TEI	composite lerfu	composite letteral follows
* foi	FOI	end composite lerfu
* lau	LAU	punctuation mark
* tau	LAU	shift next lerfu
* zai	LAU	select alphabet	2-word letteral/shift
----
I propose deprecating {ki} in favor of some longer equivalent. Maybe {[ki'i'o]} (resembling both {ki} and {ni'o}). Then maybe in a few years we can start using it for something else.

The others I don't really know much about, but it might make sense to deprecate them in the same way, encouraging a longer replacement instead.

— Daniel Brockman
 
